:: BlogPostMomMrsWng {"position":"1375,350","size":"100,100"}
The only person who ever worries about me really...is Mom. It's only Mom. But I don't want to tell her that Mason is doing this to me. It will be such a "I told you so" moment, except that my parents will say that because this isn't the first time I've ran away and not because they know what it's like to be in a gay relationship. I think Dad would care too but mom's the only one who at least asks me if I'm okay. Honestly, I think she's too clingy sometimes but at least if I die she will have something to say that isn't dismissive at the temple, ya know.

Mason had fucked me so hard on that counter, my back actually hurts. My wrists also hurt from the amount of fucking errors I made on the site.

A hard day of works makes a man unwell...


:: BlogPostNamesPackages {"position":"2050,675","size":"100,100"}
I'm required to do recycle every week and I fucking hate doing that on a rainy day. My father has been ordering all of these clocks to send to some random ass cousin in Singapore. A cousin who he doesn't give a name to but claims is related to my mom. They could be some random drug dealer for all I know who's graciously accepting my dad's gifts.

Every single one of these packages has a variant of my dad's name as the reciever of the package. I literally saw: Michael Wong, Michael Wang, Mikey Ong, Mickey Ung, Mike Jackson?? What the fuck, Dad. He's been doing this for some time but I'm only noticing it now because of how many packages he's gotten. Imagine changing your name with every package you get? Fucking psycho. 


:: BlogPostPorchNight {"position":"1300,525","size":"100,100"}
My dad was ruminating on the porch like he always does. I looked up what ruminating meant and it's exactly what he fucking does. Sometimes I don't even get much meaning out of it because it's the same yapping.

We were supposed to pay respect to the ancestors today, but my Dad decided to do it from home by lighting a candle at the shrine. His knees were hurting too much and I couldn't really give much of a shit. What gets even more on my nerves is Dad still is so unhappy that his brother was buried in the United States instead of Singapore. But he has no interest in going back to Singapore, so I don't know why he bothers whining.

Always without fail, he talks about how Uncle Jack was found dead in a car somewhere in Long Island. I even told him this time to lower it because the whole block hears him.

He just told me that he should just die because I didn't want to listen to him talk about that again for the 500th in a year. I almost threw my boot at his head but I don't want Adult Protective Services on my ass for him. Bad enough they got me in child version of the system.


:: BlogPostTeenChef {"position":"1425,475","size":"100,100"}
I know it's so not good but it just feels so right when I do it. I never stopped since the day I burned my wrist on a wok back when I was 17 and Dad was making me work in the kitchen. I don't remember what I was angry about, but I remember just searing my wrist on that shit.

It's funny because my dad has that on his wrists too but that was part of his role in the kitchen. It's a badge of honor for all his work. Me? That's just me fucking around and being fucked.


:: BlogPostThatNight1 {"position":"1375,150","size":"100,100"}
I don't want to make this too damn obvious but I don't know. I'm getting cold feet, it's like I'm getting married to the guy but I'm not. I'm 30 years old and trying to run away with a guy like I'm some 18 yr old girl running away with a suspicious guy. 

I'm leaving all my stuff here except my laptop and burner phone. Anything I need I can just buy it again. My mom and dad don't hear shit so I can run and they will think there wasn't a single sound. The old Dell laptop has missing keys and I don't care about it anymore. I don't even care if there's anything on it because it's not like my parents know how to use the laptop anyway.

When I get outside, with my bookbag all bulky like those Mainland Chinese kids on the train to Queens, for some reason the cool air and the darkness reminds me of those summer vacation days out in upstate New York.

When we would leave the hotel so early in the morning, you still think its night time. But the sky was navy blue and the sun was peeking from the envelope of darkness. The summer air would feel cool yet still. The world itself would feel like it still hasn't gotten up. My head would ache and my knees cracked. I would walk to the car and see the figure of my Dad's broad back in the front seat. His shoulders looked so big and square during that time. I would get into the car and he would always ask in this calm voice that was always unlike him and it would send me shivers because he would ask "Are you okay?"

The shivers weren't fear though. It was an ache for more of that voice he would put on. Then he would turn on the car and the radio would play the news. Now, I sent in the car with Mason and he doesn't say a single word. 


:: BlogPostTheTruckIntro {"position":"1775,550","size":"100,100"}
It is cold in here and the heat in my head can never go down. My hands tremble every time I get out of bed. But it is not exactly cold in my body, it is just here in this truck.

I know he is not here but he is not here because he wants me to cower down. I don't want to, I say this every time when I open my eyes. Yet, he is keeping me here with the expectation without literally uttering it. 

Technically it's a motor home, same shit.


:: BlogPostUnclePhoto {"position":"1425,600","size":"100,100"}
My dad is always so angry about his brother but yet I've never even met the man in my life. He just randomly started talking to me about him while I was taking my meds with food last night. I thought I was just sitting at the table alone and he just comes out in the fucking dark lurking in the kitchen like he does sometimes. To be fair, I was eating dinner at like midnight.

He told me his brother is the reason for his dad leaving. I don't know if that's true because again, I've literally never seen my uncle. I know that my dad does have a wallet with his picture in it.

My uncle stands tall in a military uniform as a teenager. The look on his face so blank, like mine in many of my family reunion pictures.


:: BlogPostWCChildhood {"position":"1650,500","size":"100,100"}
When I called the cops over, I felt myself shaking down to my knees. That was  the first time I've felt so afraid and I needed someone to hug me tight that wasn't my mom and definitely not my dad. I don't remember what happened clearly, but I know that my dad and I was fighting over something honestly stupid. 

I probably misplaced the cleaver after I cut myself with it and he started screaming because it was the golden one he likes. After the argument, I just remember myself crying in my closet, with the sun coming in through the slats and warming my knees. 

My salted tears and whatever debris on my lashes making my eyes burn. I know the droplets were falling on that big phone screen because I had one of those huge Androids. I had just called the police for a wellness check because I really, really geniunely wanted to go back. Take that cleaver and either chop off my head or behead my Dad.

The thoughts were so fucking strong. Yet, here I am posting here after I just finished sucking Mason's cock and the police alarms outside made me think of it. I had to cough out his dick so I'm apologizing after this post.


